            "review_text": "Jay Mapson\nClarksburg, California209 contributions\n0\nCulinary Enchantment by the River: Unveiling the Exquisite Delights of The Kitchen at Mia Saigon\nAug 2023 • Family\nThe Kitchen by the River at Mia Saigon unquestionably stands out as the most incredible dining experience we’ve had in all of Saigon. Under the skillful leadership of Chef Julio Gomez, the entire operation shines brightly. The staff’s professionalism and attentiveness are truly remarkable, seemingly knowing your needs before you do. Notably, managers like Sang earn respect from the staff by leading with kindness and professionalism, creating an atmosphere of genuine appreciation for staff and diners alike. \n\nThe culinary offerings are truly top-notch, accommodating both Vietnamese delicacies and Western-style dishes flawlessly. Whether you’re craving Vietnamese cuisine or Western flavors, every dish is a delight that won’t disappoint. My wife particularly adores the cảnh ca mũ and chào for breakfast, while the pho, pizzas, and burgers all stand out as equally exceptional choices.\n\nFamilies visiting from the West will find their children thanking them for choosing this establishment. The breakfast assortment is fantastic, featuring a rotating selection of hot dishes each day. Our 12-night stay was made all the more memorable by the outstanding meals we enjoyed.\n\nFor families, meals can be savored poolside, while couples are in for a treat with a romantic dinner on the most enchanting deck in Saigon. While there are other decks, none offer the unique atmosphere and overall ambience found here. Believe us, we’ve searched extensively. Treat yourself and at the very least, make a reservation for a date night dinner. It’s highly likely you’ll be tempted to book a stay before your departure after dining with Landmark 81 lit up beautifully as your backdrop and the stunning Mia Saigon and pool lit up on the other side you will have a hard time putting your phone down. Don’t worry the staff will kindly take as many pics as you’d like (tip them if you do please)! \n\nDon’t forget to explore the Muse Bar, an ideal spot for post-dinner drinks. Perched atop the hotel, it provides stunning views of the river and the splendid cityscape of Saigon.\n\nPossibly the most Instagram-able hotel overall offering the most serene and the least hectic environment in all of Saigon. \n\n10/10 Don’t miss this spot!\nRead more\nWritten August 14, 2023",
